> Module Params_2024

# Tax year 2024 parameters

Every inflation-adjusted or fixed dollar amount and rate used by more than one
rule lives here, one declaration per figure, each with its source. Page numbers
are PDF page indexes (first page = 1) of the files under `sources/`, as in
`sources/INDEX.md`. Each value was checked against the official figure in
`sources/VERIFICATION.md` on 2026-10-31 and equals the value hard-coded in the
Direct File XML (`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/`,
file named per item).

Rules (who gets which amount) do not live here; they live in the module for
their topic. Later modules add figures to this file, with the same citation
format. The rate schedules (#10), EITC table (#26), Saver's credit bands (#29),
Schedule R amounts (#30) and PTC tables (#32) are added by those issues.

## Standard deduction (IRC 63(c), Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.15)

Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.15(1), `sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` p 12. Direct File
`standardDeduction.xml`.

```catala-metadata
# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.15(1) table, rp-23-34.pdf p 12: "Married Individuals
# Filing Joint Returns and Surviving Spouses (§ 1(j)(2)(A)) $29,200".
declaration std_deduction_joint_or_surviving_spouse content money equals $29,200

# Same table: "Heads of Households (§ 1(j)(2)(B)) $21,900".
declaration std_deduction_head_of_household content money equals $21,900

# Same table: "Unmarried Individuals (other than Surviving Spouses and Heads of
# Households) (§ 1(j)(2)(C)) $14,600".
declaration std_deduction_unmarried content money equals $14,600

# Same table: "Married Individuals Filing Separate Returns (§ 1(j)(2)(D)) $14,600".
declaration std_deduction_married_separate content money equals $14,600

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.15(2), rp-23-34.pdf p 12: dependent's standard deduction
# "cannot exceed the greater of (1) $1,300, or (2) the sum of $450 and the
# individual's earned income".
declaration std_deduction_dependent_floor content money equals $1,300
declaration std_deduction_dependent_earned_income_addition content money equals $450

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.15(3), rp-23-34.pdf p 12: additional amount for the aged
# or the blind is $1,550, "increased to $1,950 if the individual is also
# unmarried and not a surviving spouse". Also i1040gi--2024.pdf p 34.
declaration std_deduction_additional_married content money equals $1,550
declaration std_deduction_additional_unmarried content money equals $1,950
```

## Dependents (IRC 152(d)(1)(B))

```catala-metadata
# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.24, rp-23-34.pdf p 14: "the exemption amount referenced
# in § 152(d)(1)(B) is $5,050". Direct File familyAndHousehold.xml
# /grossIncomeLimit (line 2664, TaxYear 2024) uses 5,050; its description
# "Rev Proc .24 Gross Income Limitation for a Qualifying Relative" names
# section .24 of the revenue procedure, i.e. this §3.24, not Rev. Proc. 2024-40.
declaration qualifying_relative_gross_income_limit content money equals $5,050
```

## Child tax credit and credit for other dependents (IRC 24)

Statute text: `sources/statute/irc-24.html`. Direct File `ctcOdc.xml`.

```catala-metadata
# IRC 24(h)(2): subsection (a) applied by substituting "$2,000" for "$1,000".
declaration ctc_per_qualifying_child content money equals $2,000

# IRC 24(h)(4)(A): "increased by $500 for each dependent ... other than a
# qualifying child".
declaration odc_per_other_dependent content money equals $500

# IRC 24(h)(3): threshold amount "$400,000 in the case of a joint return
# ($200,000 in any other case)".
declaration ctc_phaseout_threshold_joint content money equals $400,000
declaration ctc_phaseout_threshold_other content money equals $200,000

# IRC 24(b)(1): reduced "by $50 for each $1,000 (or fraction thereof)".
declaration ctc_phaseout_reduction_per_step content money equals $50
declaration ctc_phaseout_step content money equals $1,000

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.05, rp-23-34.pdf p 8: refundable portion per qualifying
# child (IRC 24(h)(5), $1,400 indexed) is $1,700.
declaration actc_per_qualifying_child_cap content money equals $1,700

# IRC 24(h)(6): (d)(1)(B)(i) applied by substituting "$2,500" for "$3,000";
# rate 15% from IRC 24(d)(1)(B)(i). Schedule 8812 lines 19-20,
# f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
declaration actc_earned_income_floor content money equals $2,500
declaration actc_earned_income_rate content decimal equals 15%
```

## Earned income credit (IRC 32)

```catala-metadata
# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.06(2), rp-23-34.pdf p 9: credit denied if aggregate
# disqualified income "exceeds $11,600". Direct File eitc.xml.
declaration eitc_investment_income_limit content money equals $11,600
```

## Child and dependent care (IRC 21, IRC 129)

Direct File `cdcc.xml`.

```catala-metadata
# IRC 21(c)(1)-(2) (sources/statute/irc-21.html): "$3,000 if there is 1
# qualifying individual"; "$6,000 if there are 2 or more".
declaration cdcc_expense_cap_one_person content money equals $3,000
declaration cdcc_expense_cap_two_or_more content money equals $6,000

# IRC 129(a)(2)(A) (sources/statute/irc-129.html): "shall not exceed $5,000
# ($2,500 in the case of a separate return by a married individual)".
declaration dependent_care_exclusion_cap content money equals $5,000
declaration dependent_care_exclusion_cap_married_separate content money equals $2,500
```

## Adjustments (Schedule 1 Part II)

```catala-metadata
# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.13, rp-23-34.pdf p 11: educator expense limit $300
# (IRC 62(a)(2)(D)). Direct File educatorAdjustment.xml.
declaration educator_expense_cap_per_educator content money equals $300

# IRC 221(b)(1) (sources/statute/irc-221.html): "shall not exceed $2,500".
# Direct File studentLoanAdjustment.xml.
declaration student_loan_interest_cap content money equals $2,500

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.30, rp-23-34.pdf p 16: phase-out "begins for taxpayers
# with modified adjusted gross income in excess of $80,000 ($165,000 for joint
# returns), and is completely phased out ... $95,000 or more ($195,000 or more
# for joint returns)".
declaration student_loan_phaseout_start_other content money equals $80,000
declaration student_loan_phaseout_start_joint content money equals $165,000
declaration student_loan_phaseout_end_other content money equals $95,000
declaration student_loan_phaseout_end_joint content money equals $195,000

# Rev. Proc. 2023-23, rp-23-23.pdf p 2: HSA annual limitation $4,150 self-only,
# $8,300 family. Direct File hsa.xml / constants.xml.
declaration hsa_limit_self_only content money equals $4,150
declaration hsa_limit_family content money equals $8,300

# IRC 223(b)(3)(B) (sources/statute/irc-223.html): additional contribution
# amount for age 55 or older is $1,000 (not indexed). i8889--2024.pdf p 4.
declaration hsa_catch_up_55 content money equals $1,000
```

## Additional Medicare Tax thresholds (W-2 knockout, issue #12)

Form 8959 line 5, `sources/forms-instructions/f8959--2024.pdf` p 1: "Enter
the following amount for your filing status: Married filing jointly $250,000,
Married filing separately $125,000, Single, Head of household, or Qualifying
surviving spouse $200,000". Direct File `formW2s.xml` `/maxMFJMedicareWages`,
`/maxMFSMedicareWages`, `/maxNonMFSorMFJMedicareWages`.

```catala-metadata
declaration additional_medicare_tax_threshold_joint content money equals $250,000
declaration additional_medicare_tax_threshold_married_separate content money equals $125,000
declaration additional_medicare_tax_threshold_other content money equals $200,000

# Same Form 8959 line 5 amount for "Single, Head of household, or Qualifying
# surviving spouse". Direct File `/maxIndividualMedicareWages` ($200,000) is the
# limit it applies to each spouse of a joint return separately.
declaration medicare_wages_individual_limit content money equals $200,000
```

## Income-side thresholds

```catala-metadata
# Pub 15 (2024), p15--2024.pdf p 2: "The social security wage base limit is
# $168,600." Direct File formW2s.xml.
declaration oasdi_wage_base content money equals $168,600

# Schedule B, f1040sb--2024.pdf p 1: "If line 4 is over $1,500, you must
# complete Part III." Direct File interest.xml /requiresScheduleB.
declaration schedule_b_interest_threshold content money equals $1,500

# IRC 86(c)(1) (sources/statute/irc-86.html): base amount "$25,000" or
# "$32,000 in the case of a joint return". 1040 instructions Social Security
# Benefits Worksheet line 8, i1040gi--2024.pdf p 32. Direct File socialSecurity.xml.
declaration ss_base_amount_other content money equals $25,000
declaration ss_base_amount_joint content money equals $32,000

# Same worksheet, line 10, i1040gi--2024.pdf p 32: "Enter $12,000 if married
# filing jointly; $9,000 if single, ...". Equal to the IRC 86(c)(2) adjusted
# base amounts ($44,000, $34,000) minus the 86(c)(1) base amounts.
declaration ss_adjusted_base_gap_other content money equals $9,000
declaration ss_adjusted_base_gap_joint content money equals $12,000

# IRC 1411(b) (sources/statute/irc-1411.html): threshold "$250,000" for a joint
# return or surviving spouse, half of that for married filing separately,
# "$200,000" in any other case. Direct File interest.xml (NIIT knockout).
declaration niit_threshold_joint_or_surviving_spouse content money equals $250,000
declaration niit_threshold_married_separate content money equals $125,000
declaration niit_threshold_other content money equals $200,000

# IRC 1341(a)(3) (sources/statute/irc-1341.html): claim-of-right relief applies
# if the deduction "exceeds $3,000". Direct File uses it as the 1099-G and
# SSA-1099 repayment knockout threshold (unemployment.xml, socialSecurity.xml).
declaration claim_of_right_threshold content money equals $3,000
```

## Schedule R (issue #30)

```catala-metadata
# Schedule R, credit for the elderly or the disabled (#30). Not indexed for
# inflation, so the same in every year (VERIFICATION.md, conventions Q9).
# IRC 22(c)(2)(A) (sources/statute/irc-22.html): initial amount "$5,000 in the
# case of a single individual, or a joint return where only one spouse is a
# qualified individual", "$7,500 in the case of a joint return where both
# spouses are qualified individuals", "$3,750 in the case of a married
# individual filing a separate return". Schedule R line 10, f1040sr--2024.pdf
# p 2. Table 1 of i1040sr--2024.pdf p 7 uses the same figures as the limit on
# nontaxable pensions ("equal to or more than").
declaration edc_initial_amount_single_or_one_qualified content money equals $5,000
declaration edc_initial_amount_joint_both_qualified content money equals $7,500
declaration edc_initial_amount_married_separate content money equals $3,750

# IRC 22(d): reduce by one-half of the excess of AGI over "$7,500" (single),
# "$10,000" (joint return), "$5,000" (married filing separately). Schedule R
# line 15, f1040sr--2024.pdf p 2.
declaration edc_agi_threshold_single content money equals $7,500
declaration edc_agi_threshold_joint content money equals $10,000
declaration edc_agi_threshold_married_separate content money equals $5,000

# i1040sr--2024.pdf p 7, Table 1: AGI "$17,500 or more" (single, HoH, QSS),
# "$20,000 or more" (joint, only one spouse qualifies), "$25,000 or more"
# (joint, both qualify), "$12,500 or more" (MFS, lived apart all year).
declaration edc_agi_limit_single_hoh_qss content money equals $17,500
declaration edc_agi_limit_joint_one_qualified content money equals $20,000
declaration edc_agi_limit_joint_both_qualified content money equals $25,000
declaration edc_agi_limit_married_separate content money equals $12,500

# IRC 22(a): "15 percent of such individual's section 22 amount" (Schedule R
# line 20). IRC 22(d): "one-half of the excess" (line 17).
declaration edc_credit_rate content decimal equals 15%
declaration edc_agi_reduction_rate content decimal equals 50%
```

## Retirement savings contributions credit, IRC 25B (issue #29)

Statute text: `sources/statute/irc-25B.html`. The dollar amounts of 25B(b)(1)
are inflation adjusted by 25B(b)(3); the TY2024 results are in Notice 2023-75
section 3 (`sources/revproc/n-23-75.pdf` p 3) and in the table on line 9 of
Form 8880 (`sources/forms-instructions/f8880--2024.pdf` p 1). Direct File
`saversCredits.xml` (`/saversCreditAgiLimitForFiftyPercent`,
`/saversCreditAgiLimitForTwentyPercent`, `/maxIncomeLimitForMFJ`,
`/maxIncomeLimitForHOH`, `/maxIncomeLimitForOther`) has the same figures.

```catala-metadata
# IRC 25B(a): contributions "as do not exceed $2,000" (not indexed). Form 8880
# line 6. DF: /saversMaxCreditLimit.
declaration savers_contribution_cap content money equals $2,000

# IRC 25B(b)(1)(A) and (b)(3), Notice 2023-75 p 3: joint return, 50 percent
# if AGI is "not over" $46,000.
declaration savers_agi_limit_50_mfj content money equals $46,000
# IRC 25B(b)(1)(B): joint return, 20 percent up to $50,000.
declaration savers_agi_limit_20_mfj content money equals $50,000
# IRC 25B(b)(1)(C): joint return, 10 percent up to $76,500.
declaration savers_agi_limit_10_mfj content money equals $76,500

# IRC 25B(b)(2)(A): head of household, 75 percent of the joint amounts as
# adjusted. Notice 2023-75 p 3: $34,500, $37,500, $57,375.
declaration savers_agi_limit_50_hoh content money equals $34,500
declaration savers_agi_limit_20_hoh content money equals $37,500
declaration savers_agi_limit_10_hoh content money equals $57,375

# IRC 25B(b)(2)(B): any other taxpayer, 50 percent of the joint amounts as
# adjusted. Notice 2023-75 p 3: $23,000, $25,000, $38,250.
declaration savers_agi_limit_50_other content money equals $23,000
declaration savers_agi_limit_20_other content money equals $25,000
declaration savers_agi_limit_10_other content money equals $38,250

# IRC 25B(b)(1)(A) to (C): the applicable percentages (not indexed).
declaration savers_rate_high content decimal equals 50%
declaration savers_rate_middle content decimal equals 20%
declaration savers_rate_low content decimal equals 10%
```

## Earned income credit: the Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06 table and the EIC Table emulation (issue #26)

IRC 32(b)(1) sets the credit and phase-out percentages; IRC 32(b)(2) and (j)
index the dollar amounts, and Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1)
(`sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` pp 8 to 9) gives the 2024 figures: "Number of
Qualifying Children: One, Two, Three or More, None; Earned Income Amount
$12,390 $17,400 $17,400 $8,260; Maximum Amount of Credit $4,213 $6,960 $7,830
$632; Threshold Phaseout Amount (Married Filing Jointly) $29,640 $29,640
$29,640 $17,250; Completed Phaseout Amount (Married Filing Jointly) $56,004
$62,688 $66,819 $25,511; Threshold Phaseout Amount (All other filing
statuses) $22,720 $22,720 $22,720 $10,330; Completed Phaseout Amount (All
other filing statuses) $49,084 $55,768 $59,899 $18,591". Direct File
`eitc.xml` carries the same numbers (`/phaseInEndsFor...`, `/eitcPhaseOutThreshold`,
`/eitcSelfLimitWith...`, `/eitcMfjLimitWith...`).

```catala-metadata
# IRC 32(b)(1) table, sources/statute/irc-32.html: credit percentage 7.65 (no
# qualifying child), 34 (1), 40 (2), 45 (3 or more).
declaration eitc_credit_percentage_0_children content decimal equals 7.65%
declaration eitc_credit_percentage_1_child content decimal equals 34%
declaration eitc_credit_percentage_2_children content decimal equals 40%
declaration eitc_credit_percentage_3_or_more_children content decimal equals 45%

# Same table: phaseout percentage 7.65 (none), 15.98 (1), 21.06 (2 or more).
declaration eitc_phaseout_percentage_0_children content decimal equals 7.65%
declaration eitc_phaseout_percentage_1_child content decimal equals 15.98%
declaration eitc_phaseout_percentage_2_or_more_children content decimal equals 21.06%

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) "Earned Income Amount": none $8,260, one
# $12,390, two or more $17,400.
declaration eitc_earned_income_amount_0_children content money equals $8,260
declaration eitc_earned_income_amount_1_child content money equals $12,390
declaration eitc_earned_income_amount_2_or_more_children content money equals $17,400

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) "Maximum Amount of Credit": $632, $4,213,
# $6,960, $7,830. Each is the credit percentage times the earned income amount
# rounded to the dollar (Direct File computes `Round(rate * amount)`); the
# tests check this.
declaration eitc_max_credit_0_children content money equals $632
declaration eitc_max_credit_1_child content money equals $4,213
declaration eitc_max_credit_2_children content money equals $6,960
declaration eitc_max_credit_3_or_more_children content money equals $7,830

# Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) "Threshold Phaseout Amount (All other filing
# statuses)": $10,330 with no qualifying child, $22,720 with one or more. The
# note under the table applies the "all other" column also to "married
# taxpayers who are not filing a joint return and satisfy the special rules
# for separated spouses in § 32(d)".
declaration eitc_phaseout_threshold_other_0_children content money equals $10,330
declaration eitc_phaseout_threshold_other_1_or_more_children content money equals $22,720

# Same table, "(Married Filing Jointly)": $17,250 and $29,640.
declaration eitc_phaseout_threshold_joint_0_children content money equals $17,250
declaration eitc_phaseout_threshold_joint_1_or_more_children content money equals $29,640

# Same table, "Completed Phaseout Amount (All other filing statuses)":
# $18,591, $49,084, $55,768, $59,899 for none, one, two, three or more.
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_other_0_children content money equals $18,591
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_other_1_child content money equals $49,084
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_other_2_children content money equals $55,768
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_other_3_or_more_children content money equals $59,899

# Same table, "Completed Phaseout Amount (Married Filing Jointly)":
# $25,511, $56,004, $62,688, $66,819.
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_0_children content money equals $25,511
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_1_child content money equals $56,004
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_2_children content money equals $62,688
declaration eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_3_or_more_children content money equals $66,819

# IRC 32(f)(2): the tables "shall ... have income brackets of not greater than
# $50 each". The 2024 EIC Table (i1040gi--2024.pdf pp 46 to 56) has rows
# "At least X, but less than X + $50". Direct File evaluates the formula at the
# middle of the row: `StepwiseMultiply(x, 50/50) + $25`
# (eitc.xml /eitcRoundedEarnedIncomeWithoutCombatPay), and decides whether the
# row reaches the maximum credit at its last whole dollar, `+ $24`
# (/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay). The row width is the `50` of the 50/50 rate.
declaration eitc_table_row_width content integer equals 50
declaration eitc_table_row_midpoint content money equals $25
declaration eitc_table_row_last_dollar_offset content money equals $24
```

## Child and dependent care credit: further constants (IRC 21; Form 2441)

Added by issue #28; the dollar caps and exclusion limits are declared above.
Direct File `cdcc.xml`.

```catala-metadata
# IRC 21(a)(2) (sources/statute/irc-21.html): "35 percent reduced (but not
# below 20 percent) by 1 percentage point for each $2,000 (or fraction
# thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year
# exceeds $15,000". None of these figures is indexed. Form 2441 line 8 table
# (f2441--2024.pdf p 1; i2441--2024.pdf p 7 for Worksheet A): .35 up to
# $15,000, then .34, .33, ... in $2,000 steps, .20 over $43,000.
# DF cdcc.xml /cdccMaxAllowedPercentageTY2024 (35), /cdccMinAllowedPercentageTY2024
# (20), /cdccCareExpensesFallOffThreshold ($15,000), /cdccCareExpensesPlateauThreshold
# ($43,000).
declaration cdcc_maximum_percentage content decimal equals 35%
declaration cdcc_minimum_percentage content decimal equals 20%
declaration cdcc_percentage_reduction_threshold content money equals $15,000
declaration cdcc_percentage_step_income content money equals $2,000
declaration cdcc_percentage_step content decimal equals 1%

# IRC 21(d)(2) (sources/statute/irc-21.html): a student or incapable spouse
# "shall be deemed for each month ... to be gainfully employed and to have
# earned income of not less than (A) $250 if subsection (c)(1) applies for the
# taxable year, or (B) $500 if subsection (c)(2) applies". Not indexed.
# DF income.xml /cdccDisabledOrInSchoolIncomePerMonthWithOneQp ($250) and
# /cdccDisabledOrInSchoolIncomePerMonthWithMultipleQps ($500).
declaration cdcc_deemed_monthly_income_one_person content money equals $250
declaration cdcc_deemed_monthly_income_two_or_more content money equals $500

# IRC 21(b)(1)(A): "a dependent of the taxpayer ... who has not attained age
# 13". DF familyAndHousehold.xml /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccTurnedThirteenAfterJanFirst.
declaration cdcc_qualifying_child_age_limit content integer equals 13
```
